1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:04,400
欢迎来到我们策略演练的最后一场
Welcome to the final of our drill sessions.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:09,340
这是策略10，单元15，主题是风险事件
This is strategy 10, unit 15, which is all about risk events.

4
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:12,620
我之前给大家展示了两个典型风险事件
I did show you two really cool risk events.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:18,240
一个是特朗普-弗林事件，另一个是欧元CPI
One was the Trump-Flynn saga, and then the Euro CPI.

7
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:22,731
我认为这些风险事件的核心以及希望大家能领悟的关键要点就是一切都在于准备
I think the gist of these risk events and the real key takeaway

8
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:27,438
that hopefully you all picked up on is that it’s all about preparation.

11
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:31,640
每一个细节都取决于准备
Every single thing comes down to preparation.

12
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:35,100
交易者必须准备市场背景
You need to prepare the context of your market.

13
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:39,640
必须充分理解风险事件前的市场状态
You need to have a good understanding of where your market is trading going into that risk event.

16
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:44,540
若要总结风险事件的本质它会迫使参与者比平时更快做出反应
If I was to summarize what a risk event is, in essence,

17
00:00:44,540 --> 00:00:49,040
it forces participants to respond and react quicker than they normally would.

20
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:54,200
为什么？因为数据或公告推动价格
Why? Because the data or the announcement or whatever it might be pushes prices to a point

23
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:56,460
到更多参与者必须响应的点位
where a lot more participants have to respond.

24
00:00:56,580 --> 00:00:57,900
这正是交易者必须识别的
And that’s what you have to recognize.

25
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:00,816
风险事件带来机会因为它迫使策略加速执行而非在无数据时缓慢推进
These risk events bring opportunities simply because

26
00:01:00,816 --> 00:01:05,972
they force the strategies to come a lot quicker than they would have

27
00:01:05,972 --> 00:01:07,558
otherwise without the data.

29
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:14,400
我们来分析12月英国通胀数据
So what we’re going to look at is the UK inflation data in December.

31
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:22,060
市场预期为3%，实际低0.1%
It was expected to come out at 3% And it actually came out 0.1% lower than expected. Now, it was important

33
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:24,320
这很重要，因英央行（Bank of England）的立场
Simply because of where the Bank of England’s stance was.

34
00:01:24,740 --> 00:01:27,320
最近刚加息
There was just recently a hike

35
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:33,000
市场正试图判断下次加息时间
And the market was trying to figure out when that next potential rate hike could come.

37
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:35,660
现在，重点是我们要回放这一过程
Now, the important thing is, we’re going to play this through.

39
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:42,635
我想强调的是，足迹图对风险事件交易的价值因为市场参与者越少，流动性越低就越容易发现首个吸纳出现的时机
And all I want to reference is, the reason why the footprint is so fantastic for risk event trading

40
00:01:42,635 --> 00:01:47,407
is simply because, The fewer participants in the market and the less liquidity,

41
00:01:47,407 --> 00:01:55,117
the easier it is to ultimately see and pick up when that first bit of absorption actually comes into the market.

46
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:58,333
我们再来看，我们会逐步分析最终会看到快速资金下行
So, again, what we’re going to see, we’re going to talk through,

47
00:01:58,333 --> 00:02:00,858
We’re ultimately going to see that fast money move down.

49
00:02:01,620 --> 00:02:05,320
但交易者很难参与其中
Again, very unlikely that you’re ever going to be able to partake in this,

51
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:08,868
因为这必须是一个真正的异常值
Simply because it would need to be a real outlier.

52
00:02:08,868 --> 00:02:14,190
所以我们说，要抓住趋势性行情你需要一个真正强劲的异常值信息
So we said, in order to be aggressive, in order to get those trend-type moves,

53
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:17,738
you would require a real strong piece of outlier information.

54
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:24,440
在这个例子中，偏差0.2%或0.3%才算异常值
So in this example, I would say anything 0.2% or 0.3% of a miss would have been an outlier.

57
00:02:24,860 --> 00:02:30,500
但实际仅出现0.1%的异常值。好，数据公布后——
Obviously, it only came out as a 0.1% outlier. Okay, so again—bang—we hear the number,

58
00:02:30,600 --> 00:02:33,700
数据公布为0.1%，我们看到初始反应
The number comes up 0.1% and we see the initial reaction.

60
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:37,829
非常快，50个Tick闪现，没有真正的入场机会
Very quick, 50-tick blip, no real opportunity to get involved there.

61
00:02:37,829 --> 00:02:42,519
但我们意识到，首次回调往往至关重要
Okay, we did, however, recognize that the first pullback is always quite crucial.

64
00:02:45,460 --> 00:02:48,321
现在看右侧的足迹图我们寻找首个吸收迹象
So, what we're looking at on this footprint on the right side

65
00:02:48,321 --> 00:02:50,466
is we're looking for that first bit of absorption.

66
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,820
卖家同时吸收并抛售
a seller to absorb as well as a seller at the same time.

68
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,440
一旦发现，我们将尝试在空头方向入场并寻求测试前低点
The moment we see that, we're going to try and enter on the short side

69
00:02:58,440 --> 00:02:59,480
and try and look for a retest of the lows.

71
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:09,420
市场回升。注意成交量：15手、6手、9手、22手，交易清淡
Okay, so the market comes back bid. Note what we're seeing: 15 lots, 6 lots, 9 lots, 22. Not a great deal traded there.

73
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:14,034
前高点是04价位。流动性依然稀缺
The top was 04s. Now, again, remember, liquidity is still very much at a premium.

74
00:03:14,034 --> 00:03:16,019
所以市场才会如此清淡
That's why the markets are so thin.

76
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:21,200
为确保安全，我们需要看到更多吸收
So, to safeguard ourselves, we do want to see a little more absorption.

77
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:24,680
看，这里出现了。注意立即出现的：111手
And there we can see it. Okay, notice straight away what's coming in: 111.

78
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:28,511
我们看到什么？在卖价吸收，但同时在最优买价抛售
What are we seeing? Absorbing on the offer, but equally selling at the best bid.

79
00:03:28,511 --> 00:03:30,299
好，吸收正在发生
Okay, so there's our absorption taking place.

80
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:36,245
现在我们入场交易。在00或01价位入场
We now enter our trade. We want to enter at the 00s, at the 01s,

81
00:03:36,245 --> 00:03:39,919
即吸收发生的位置，寻求测试前低点并可能延伸
where that absorption took place, looking for a retest of the lows and potentially an extension.

84
00:03:46,020 --> 00:03:47,728
注意这里也有吸收：58手再次交易就在吸收发生的位置。这是一个很好的例子
Again, note a little bit of absorption there:

85
00:03:47,728 --> 00:03:49,863
58 contracts trade again, side by side, where that absorption was.

86
00:03:49,863 --> 00:03:52,638
Okay, so, really good example of how you can see nothing going on

88
00:03:56,120 --> 00:04:00,329
看似无事发生，但足迹图能突出显示首次回调的吸收
and suddenly the footprint can really highlight where that absorption comes in on the first pullback.

89
00:04:00,329 --> 00:04:03,485
随后市场开始出现卖盘。这点很关键
Okay, the market then starts to offer. And this is quite crucial.

90
00:04:03,485 --> 00:04:07,054
当市场识别出成交量密集区或吸收区后由于市场清淡，会迅速再次下行
When the market has identified that volume pocket or that absorption,

91
00:04:07,054 --> 00:04:09,974
it will tend to offer very quickly down again

92
00:04:12,572 --> 00:04:15,839
在K线图上也能看到
We can see it on the candlestick as well.

93
00:04:16,560 --> 00:04:24,100
注意，此轮回调的成交量仍相对合理，Delta表现良好
Do note, still relatively okay volume on that rotation. Good delta in relative terms.

95
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:29,100
但重点仍是评估数据的关键性
But again, this is where assessing the data is crucial.

97
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,475
若数据偏差0.2%，则下跌概率会大幅提升远高于实际偏差0.1%的情形
Had this number been a 0.2 miss,

98
00:04:31,475 --> 00:04:34,986
we would have had a much higher probability of extending lower

99
00:04:34,986 --> 00:04:38,178
than if it was just a 0.1 miss, as we got.

100
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:41,420
随后市场形成一个小型内包K线
Okay, so the market then obviously forms a little inside candle.

101
00:04:41,420 --> 00:04:45,240
出现小幅延伸，并测试前期低点
We do get a little extension, a little test of the previous low.

103
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:51,300
市场形成双底，随即开始拍卖回升
Market double-bottoms, and straight away we begin to auction back higher.

105
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:55,680
市场随即走高，大部分交易者已熟悉此案例
Okay, the market then goes. I mean, most of you have been through this example now.

107
00:04:55,920 --> 00:05:02,140
价格回升，重新测试衰竭点或吸收区域
It does come back up. It retests that point of exhaustion or the absorption that we identified

110
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:04,580
之后再次回落
and then offers back down again.

111
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:10,374
本视频不再展开过多细节因为我们已明确风险事件交易的核心要素
Now, I don’t really want to go over too much more in this video,

112
00:05:10,374 --> 00:05:15,308
simply because, we’ve identified what the real key element to risk event trading is.

113
00:05:15,308 --> 00:05:20,899
第一，明确异常值与预期值的区别
It’s about, number one, making sure you know what the outliers are versus what’s expected.

116
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,860
构建二元逻辑
Okay, you create the binary.

117
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,960
这是掌握该策略的关键
That’s the real key to getting good at this strategy.

118
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:27,128
在头脑中构建二元逻辑
You create the binary in your head.

119
00:05:27,128 --> 00:05:32,039
要么A发生，执行A；要么B发生，执行B
It either does A and you execute A or it does B and you execute B.

121
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:33,480
策略就是这么简单
It is as simple as that.

122
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:40,100
明确异常值后，再理解市场所处的背景
Once you have an understanding of what those outliers are, you simply understand the context in which your market is.

126
00:05:40,240 --> 00:05:42,300
关键支撑阻力位在哪里？
Where are the key support and resistance?

127
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:45,720
市场的关键节点在哪？是否有台阶？
Where are the key pinch points in the market? Are there some ledges?

128
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:50,920
市场因失衡而激进，还是趋于平衡？
Is this market likely to be aggressive because it is imbalanced or is it likely to be balanced?

130
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:59,540
将准备工作细化，市场反应时直接执行
You really just break down the preparation so that when the market responds and suddenly moves, you simply execute.

